1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,040
Miss Tai, you need to understand,

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:05,560
only you know what happened to
the victim.

3
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:07,600
I only took the gas cylinder
from his backpack

4
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:09,600
I don't know anything else.

5
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:11,960
What did you give Jarvis, you bloody witch?

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,840
You killed him...

7
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:18,720
It got out of hand.

8
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:20,480
There's no turning back now.

9
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:28,160
(Three months after the incident)

10
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:30,000
The kids from Agent J knew about

11
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:32,080
Ngai Ka-yan's death and the stink bomb.

12
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:33,840
Something is not right.

13
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,240
They renamed the livestreaming
"Live from Sorry Sir".

14
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:40,080
They're obviously showing off
they had you surrounded.

15
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:42,080
They're a team.

16
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:45,600
The kid I was chasing was their head.

17
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:47,760
Did you notice anything else?

18
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:50,960
No. They were really fast.

19
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:52,360
I didn't see anything.

20
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:54,840
They even knew I go by Gogo Sir.

21
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:58,840
They're definitely connected to
Ngai Ka-yan's death.

22
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:01,000
(The day of the incident)

23
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:13,160
What happened? How come...

24
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:15,120
What did you give Jarvis, you bloody witch?

25
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:16,480
Oxygen.

26
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:18,000
Oxygen wouldn't have killed Jarvis!

27
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:19,680
You killed him...

28
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:21,360
Hey, stop it!

29
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:31,080
Get out of my way...
Calm down!

30
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:32,560
She killed Jarvis...

31
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:34,760
It's her...Jarvis is gone!
Listen to me...

32
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:37,600
Get away from me...it's her!
Calm down...

33
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:43,720
Hello! We're from the Crime Unit,
New Territories East.

34
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:48,040
Oh...what is it, Officer?

35
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:50,040
During the livestreaming of
the Static Apnea Challenge,

36
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:52,880
director Ngai Ka-yan died from
inhaling a dangerous gas.

37
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,360
We're here to gather evidence.

38
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:55,960
Jarvis is dead?!

39
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:58,640
What happened?

40
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:01,120
Calm down...what should we call you?

41
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:04,720
I'm Yuen Kit-ching. I'm the cleaning lady.

42
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:07,360
Auntie Ching, can you show us
Ngai Ka-yan's office?

43
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:11,800
It's over there, but he went out.

44
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:16,040
The door is locked, you need to
wait for him...

45
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:19,720
How did he die?

46
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:21,800
Do you have a spare key?

47
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:25,960
I think he had the only key.

48
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:27,600
Cheong, call and find out

49
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:30,120
if Ngai Ka-yan had the key on him.

50
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:16,400
Mr. Tsang Chun-kit,

51
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:18,240
according to people at the scene,

52
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:20,720
you and your partner Hung Tzi-long
were responsible for

53
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:25,280
the oxygen cylinders used in
the Static Apnea Challenge,

54
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:28,400
including the one Ngai Ka-yan
inhaled from, is that right?

55
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:31,640
Please answer the question.

56
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:33,080
Yes.

57
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:36,160
But on the bench next to the pool,

58
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:38,120
we collected 20 portable oxygen cylinders.

59
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:41,080
After testing, they do not contain oxygen,

60
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:42,680
but hydrogen sulfide (H2S),

61
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:44,680
or what we call a stink bomb.

62
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:46,360
(For Static Apnea Challenge)

63
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:52,480
Hung Tzi-long, in a unit on the 18/F
of Hing Fong Factory Building,

64
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:54,520
this is what we found.

65
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:57,840
Did you use it to make stink bombs
with Tsang Chun-kit?

66
00:04:58,680 --> 00:04:59,960
Yes.

67
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:03,160
We made 20 cylinders

68
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:05,320
to pull a prank on Jarvis.

69
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:09,200
OK! You said you were making stink bombs.

70
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:13,240
But inside the cylinder Ngai Ka-yan used,

71
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:16,440
our Forensics colleagues found
over 1000 ppm of H2S.

72
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:19,680
That was a lethal dosage.

73
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:25,080
Low concentration of H2S will only
smell like rotten egg.

74
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:27,160
That's why they call it a stink bomb.

75
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:30,440
It will only cause slight discomfort.

76
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:32,560
But a high concentration is different,

77
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:34,080
it becomes colorless and odorless.

78
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:36,400
A whiff of it can knock you out

79
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:39,280
and may even be lethal.

80
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:41,840
I didn't know the concentration
was that high.

81
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,160
I only followed Tom's formula to make
the stink bombs.

82
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:47,160
I'm quite sure about the quantity.

83
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:50,280
It was meant to be a prank on Jarvis.

84
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:53,000
For the livestreaming of the Challenge,

85
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:55,960
Ngai Ka-yan decided to do it himself
the last minute.

86
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:57,640
Then he died suddenly.

87
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:59,600
Your colleagues told us

88
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:02,400
you had a run-in with Ngai Ka-yan
over filming

89
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:04,160
and you resented him.

90
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:06,880
In terms of motive and murder weapon,

91
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:08,560
you're the prime suspect.

92
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:10,760
We'd like to hear your explanation.

93
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:13,440
Sir, I never meant to kill Jarvis.

94
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:16,000
I know why you think I have a motive.

95
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:19,360
But everyone knew we didn't get along,

96
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:22,560
why would I brazenly kill him

97
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:25,520
in front of everyone during a livestreaming?

98
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:47,120
What happened?

99
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:49,560
We followed the formula to
make the stink bombs.

100
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:51,800
Everything checked out.

101
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:54,680
I don't know what happened.

102
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:58,040
Why is Jarvis dead?

103
00:06:58,200 --> 00:07:01,000
We may not get along lately,

104
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:04,880
but I still remember how
he helped us back then.

105
00:07:04,960 --> 00:07:05,840
(Two years ago)

106
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:09,400
Peter Piper picked a peck of
pickled peppers.

107
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:14,080
She sells seashells by the seashore.

108
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:19,640
Folks, you just saw how good Hongkongers
are with tongue twisters.

109
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:21,840
If you want to watch more street games,

110
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:23,680
remember to CLS, comment, like
and share this video.

111
00:07:23,760 --> 00:07:25,600
See you next time.

112
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:29,560
You're shooting for an online channel.

113
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:31,040
Speaking like a pro.

114
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:34,240
Here's your agreed pay.

115
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:37,600
But...$2,000 is hardly enough.

116
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:39,960
I have loads of other games.

117
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:41,240
If you're interested,

118
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:46,040
I can raise your pay to $20K.

119
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:49,520
This game is simple.

120
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:51,320
You see two buckets up there.

121
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:55,480
One is clear water, the other is watercolor.

122
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,680
I don't care how,

123
00:07:57,840 --> 00:07:59,560
if you pick the bucket of water,

124
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:02,000
the $20K is yours.

125
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:04,440
But if you picked the watercolor,

126
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:07,360
sorry, kiss the money goodbye.

127
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:11,240
50/50? That's tough.

128
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:14,040
Wait, we'll pull the rope together.

129
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:16,200
One of us will get it right.

130
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:18,200
Then we can split the money.

131
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:19,600
One on each side?

132
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:20,960
Of course!

133
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:23,200
Any way we want?

134
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:24,240
Yes!

135
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:25,640
Deal!

136
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:31,480
Almost...get a close up.

137
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:41,720
Go get him...

138
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:44,880
Look...a blade of grass!

139
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:47,880
This way...a tissue!

140
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:50,320
Hey...how do you feel? Cold? Comfy?

141
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:52,040
You jerk!

142
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:53,160
Chill!

143
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:57,600
You want money, right? Here's $100K.

144
00:08:57,720 --> 00:08:59,560
Have fun picking them up.

145
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:08,400
Finders keepers.

146
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:12,200
Folks, time flies and it's the end
of our livestreaming.

147
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:14,600
You think they made out like a bandit?

148
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:16,480
I'll let you in on a secret.

149
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:18,440
It's fake money.

150
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:21,280
Stay tuned to J Weekly.

151
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:24,280
Don't forget to like, comment and share.

152
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:26,320
See you next time. Bye!

153
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:31,200
It's fake money.

154
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:34,520
That's enough! You poured pigswill on us

155
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:35,600
and gave us fake money.

156
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:37,080
We need a gimmick in our video

157
00:09:37,120 --> 00:09:40,280
to attract viewers. Look at them...

158
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:45,800
Here's your $20K. All yours.

159
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:48,000
This time for real.

160
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:52,320
Forget it.

161
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:55,360
We spent less than an hour. Forget it.

162
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:57,640
Jarvis, in ten minutes,

163
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,000
we have over 10K views

164
00:09:59,080 --> 00:10:00,200
and 10K likes.

165
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:01,760
They said it's very entertaining

166
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:03,440
and those two are hilarious.

167
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:05,440
They said you're smart.

168
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:09,560
By the way, I'm Jarvis.

169
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:11,600
The creator and director of J Weekly.

170
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:14,440
We'll be filming more pranks.

171
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:17,040
You guys have quick reflexes
and are a good sport.

172
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:20,880
Would you like to join us and make money?

173
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:26,440
Shake on it and we're friends.

174
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:28,360
Don't con us with fake money again.

175
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:36,400
Your turn...

176
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:38,200
What are you doing? Get away from me!

177
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:41,600
Give me a hand. Who's paying you?

178
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:53,720
(J Weekly)

179
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:55,920
Can you just lift his legs?
Sure!

180
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:58,240
Thanks. Ready? 3...2...1...pull!

181
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:02,520
What? You tore off his legs!

182
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:03,680
What are you doing?

183
00:11:03,760 --> 00:11:04,720
Stop filming.

184
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,440
I got it!

185
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:16,960
Let's check the replay.

186
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:18,880
Cheers!

187
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:24,760
This office is huge and awesome.

188
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:28,880
Jarvis, your backer must be loaded.

189
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,640
Our channel gathered a lot of followers

190
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:32,800
and people are topping up.

191
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:34,280
The Boss should be pleased.

192
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:36,040
You're the brilliant one, Jarvis.

193
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:37,320
Even bit part actors like us

194
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:39,840
are now recognized by people on the street.

195
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:41,280
I can bring glory to the family.

196
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:43,640
Wait...you're the bit part actor, not me.

197
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:45,560
Quit bickering...
You're the one...

198
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:50,840
Your work brought J Weekly to new heights.

199
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:53,840
Here's your share of the money.

200
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:55,240
Thanks, Jarvis!
Thanks.

201
00:11:55,440 --> 00:11:57,440
Peter, this is for you.

202
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,000
Auntie Ching...

203
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:02,440
For me?

204
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:06,600
Thanks!

205
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:09,040
It'll take longer to clean a bigger place.

206
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:11,640
I hope you'll keep expanding.

207
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:13,200
Thanks.

208
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:15,400
I'll make sweet soup for you.

209
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:17,160
Thanks.
Thanks, Auntie Ching.

210
00:12:19,560 --> 00:12:23,640
Folks, this is just the beginning.

211
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:27,320
We'll be making much more.

212
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:30,200
Jarvis, how much more? (Hiccup)

213
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:34,360
I like the sound of that.

214
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:40,840
Let's aim for the homophone of a hiccup.

215
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:41,480
A hiccup?

216
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:42,120
A hiccup?

217
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:42,720
A hiccup?

218
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:43,760
A hiccup?

219
00:12:43,840 --> 00:12:44,880
100 million?

220
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:48,160
100 million!

221
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:52,280
The jerk is ruthless to toy with
one of ours.

222
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:57,080
He's the scumbag, remember?

223
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:00,560
Ngai Ka-yan, you set me up?

224
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:02,360
What are you talking about?

225
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:04,280
You claimed to let me run a new channel.

226
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:06,000
That was just the bait to set me up.

227
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:08,040
Why would I do that?

228
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:09,440
Because you're jealous.

229
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:12,320
You're scared we would surpass you
and replace you.

230
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:14,200
That's why you're desperate.

231
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:16,560
Will Jarvis fall for it?

232
00:13:16,760 --> 00:13:19,280
He already put on half of his wetsuit.

233
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:21,840
It got out of hand.

234
00:13:22,560 --> 00:13:24,400
There's no turning back now.

235
00:13:32,160 --> 00:13:36,280
Miss Tai Yat-sze, we have questions for you.

236
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:40,720
Before anything happened to Ngai Ka-yan,

237
00:13:40,800 --> 00:13:42,920
you handed him a blue cylinder,

238
00:13:43,040 --> 00:13:46,200
he inhaled from it and passed out.

239
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:47,640
What else do you know?

240
00:13:47,760 --> 00:13:51,040
Sir, Jarvis asked me to take a gas cylinder

241
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:53,440
he prepared for himself from his backpack.

242
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:59,880
Ngai Ka-yan prepared it
for himself beforehand?

243
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:04,160
No wonder Tsang Chun-kit insisted
he only made 20 cylinders,

244
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:06,720
but we found 21 at the scene.

245
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:11,520
Ngan Ka-yan couldn't have prepared
a gas cylinder to kill himself.

246
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:14,280
I don't know how it happened...

247
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:17,720
Why did he ask you to take
the cylinder from his backpack?

248
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:21,680
He said Tom and Paul are traitors.

249
00:14:22,280 --> 00:14:26,680
Those two ingrates planned to trick me
with a stink bomb during the livestreaming.

250
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:29,440
But I prepared a real oxygen cylinder
for myself.

251
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:31,440
I'll play dead after I inhale from it

252
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:33,400
and scare the crap out of them.

253
00:14:33,480 --> 00:14:36,600
That's why I took the cylinder
from his backpack like he said.

254
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:38,400
I held onto it the whole time,

255
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:40,360
to make sure I won't mix them up.

256
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:43,640
Then I handed it to Jarvis
during the livestreaming.

257
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:45,720
The killer obviously knew beforehand

258
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:48,120
Ngai Ka-yan prepared a real
oxygen cylinder for himself,

259
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:52,320
and waited for a chance to swap it
with a high concentration of H2S.

260
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:54,440
Miss Tai, you need to understand,

261
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:57,720
only you know what happened to the victim.

262
00:14:57,840 --> 00:15:00,040
I only took the gas cylinder
from his backpack

263
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:02,160
I don't know anything else.

264
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:04,200
If you don't believe me,

265
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:06,800
you can check out my chat with Jarvis.

266
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:09,960
I bought it but I want to take it back
to the office.

267
00:15:10,040 --> 00:15:11,480
I'll come over after I drop it off.

268
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:13,080
I'm done. I'm coming.

269
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:15,000
Thanks.

270
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:18,160
I remember when he arrived
at the restaurant,

271
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:21,080
it was around 12:15 p.m.,

272
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:24,120
and he didn't have the backpack.

273
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:25,960
Before you head out to the pool.

274
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:27,400
what else did you do?

275
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:30,120
We had lunch till 2 o'clock,

276
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:32,760
then went back to his office.

277
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:35,320
He put the blue cylinder in his backpack

278
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:37,920
and we headed out to the pool.

279
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:41,760
At 11:30 a.m., Ngai Ka-yan went out to
buy the cylinder,

280
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:44,160
then drop it off at the office.

281
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:47,920
He had lunch with Tai Yat-sze
at around noon.

282
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:50,040
Between noon and 2 p.m.,

283
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:53,600
Ngai Ka-yan left the cylinder in his office.

284
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:57,560
At 2 p.m. he went back to get it and
pick up his backpack.

285
00:15:57,640 --> 00:16:02,040
Tai Yat-sze said Ngai Ka-yan took the
cylinder from the cabinet,

286
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:06,320
but that day when we were searching
Ngai Ka-yan's office,

287
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:10,120
I found another blue cylinder
behind a figurine.

288
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:15,480
Both blue cylinders were identical.

289
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,640
In the Forensics report,

290
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:20,200
the victim inhaled from the one
with a high concentration of H2S.

291
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:23,440
The one found in his office was pure oxygen.

292
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:26,440
The other 20 were low concentration of H2S.

293
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:29,560
The killer swapped the high concentration
of H2S with the pure oxygen.

294
00:16:29,760 --> 00:16:31,560
Between noon and 2 p.m.,

295
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:35,160
is the window for the killer to swap
the two cylinders.

296
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:38,680
Bring in everyone from the online channel
for questioning.

297
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:40,280
I checked with the staff,

298
00:16:40,320 --> 00:16:41,680
Peter, the PA and Modem, the I.T. guy

299
00:16:41,760 --> 00:16:44,400
went down to the pool early for set up.

300
00:16:44,520 --> 00:16:47,800
The rest of the staff,
headed out to the pool at 2 p.m.

301
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:53,640
Miss Lam Sum-ling,

302
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:58,360
between noon and 2 p.m. on the day
of the incident,

303
00:16:58,480 --> 00:16:59,600
where were you and what were you doing?

304
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:01,840
I was doing a livestreaming with Paul

305
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:06,400
