inside the office together.

408
00:21:16,920 --> 00:21:19,680
Then Wendy came out of the pantry.

409
00:21:19,800 --> 00:21:24,200
And Paul came from the supplies room
with some props.

410
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:27,680
Go down for the set up. I'll be down later.

411
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:40,840
According to the four of them,

412
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:42,280
at 1:50 p.m. on that day,

413
00:21:42,360 --> 00:21:44,000
that's what happened at the office.

414
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:46,640
We're missing someone.

415
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:49,080
Tai Yat-sze.

416
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:52,160
After Jarvis and I finished lunch,

417
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:53,920
he drove me back to his office.

418
00:21:54,040 --> 00:21:56,360
He said he wanted a smoke in the parking lot

419
00:21:56,480 --> 00:21:58,960
and I had a slight bellyache,

420
00:21:59,040 --> 00:22:00,680
so I went up to use the toilet.

421
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:02,760
Was there anyone else inside?

422
00:22:03,800 --> 00:22:06,040
Not when I went in.

423
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:10,360
Inside the stall, I heard the door
opened and closed.

424
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:12,560
Someone must have come in and went out.

425
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:17,640
Do you remember how long it was
between the door opening and closing?

426
00:22:17,840 --> 00:22:19,240
I'm not sure.

427
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:23,200
But there was no one there
when I came out of the stall.

428
00:22:23,320 --> 00:22:26,360
Other than the door opening and closing,
did you hear anything else?

429
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:28,880
No!

430
00:22:29,080 --> 00:22:30,800
Then what happened?

431
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:33,080
Like I told you before,

432
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:36,680
Jarvis took a blue cylinder from a drawer

433
00:22:36,760 --> 00:22:38,000
and put it in his backpack.

434
00:22:38,080 --> 00:22:40,440
Then he grabbed the backpack, locked up

435
00:22:40,600 --> 00:22:42,640
and headed for the pool.

436
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:47,280
Everything they said fits,
with no contradictions.

437
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:49,600
But timewise, we have blind spots.

438
00:22:49,720 --> 00:22:50,880
Blind spots?

439
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:54,040
Tai Yat-sze said she heard the door
open and close,

440
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:56,560
Wendy came in, Wendy went out.

441
00:22:56,720 --> 00:22:59,200
But after Wendy left,
did she go straight to the panty?

442
00:22:59,320 --> 00:23:00,440
Nobody knows.

443
00:23:00,560 --> 00:23:03,320
Wendy could prove Hung Tzi-long
went into the conference room,

444
00:23:03,400 --> 00:23:06,200
and he met Tsang Chun-kit in the hallway,

445
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:09,320
but how long was Tsang Chun-kit
in the supplies room?

446
00:23:09,440 --> 00:23:11,400
Nobody can vouch for that.

447
00:23:11,520 --> 00:23:14,720
They all had an alibi at some point,

448
00:23:14,880 --> 00:23:16,680
Tsang Chun-kit ran into Hung Tzi-long,

449
00:23:16,760 --> 00:23:18,600
but how long was he in the toilet?

450
00:23:18,800 --> 00:23:19,800
And Yuen Kit-ching...

451
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:21,320
when we showed up to search for evidence,

452
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:24,120
there was a pot of sweet soup in the pantry,

453
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:25,880
but how long was she there?

454
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,640
Nobody could confirm.

455
00:23:27,760 --> 00:23:29,240
And someone was lying.

456
00:23:29,520 --> 00:23:32,120
Someone who made use of
the blind spot in time,

457
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:36,120
went inside Ngai Ka-yan's office
and swapped the cylinders.

458
00:23:43,920 --> 00:23:47,160
Wendy, can you go with me to see
Cigarette To the day after tomorrow?

459
00:23:47,240 --> 00:23:49,160
I need to discuss something with you.

460
00:23:49,280 --> 00:23:50,520
Jarvis?

461
00:23:54,160 --> 00:23:56,880
(120 minute review of Chief J's
classic pranks)

462
00:24:01,120 --> 00:24:02,760
The first time I saw Jarvis' videos,

463
00:24:02,880 --> 00:24:04,360
was four years ago Christmas.

464
00:24:04,960 --> 00:24:07,960
Jarvis' pranks on a loving couple
along the harbor front

465
00:24:08,040 --> 00:24:09,280
really made my day.

466
00:24:09,360 --> 00:24:11,480
He let off a stink bomb in the subway,

467
00:24:11,560 --> 00:24:13,240
he also livestreamed a prank on the cops.

468
00:24:13,320 --> 00:24:15,200
He came away unscathed even
after he was arrested.

469
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:17,920
I dare say in the dotcom world,

470
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:20,680
Jarvis is the most creative and
daring creator.

471
00:24:22,360 --> 00:24:24,880
We narrowed down the window
for the swap to ten minutes.

472
00:24:25,120 --> 00:24:27,600
But we had no idea how to proceed.

473
00:24:27,960 --> 00:24:30,560
All five of them collaborated
on their statements?

474
00:24:30,600 --> 00:24:31,680
That's why they're flawless?

475
00:24:31,760 --> 00:24:33,320
Doesn't look like it.

476
00:24:33,400 --> 00:24:35,520
But someone is lying.

477
00:24:35,920 --> 00:24:38,120
Let's start checking their backgrounds.

478
00:24:39,560 --> 00:24:42,600
Who broke the mug? Fess up!

479
00:24:42,840 --> 00:24:44,920
Not me...watch where you're going.

480
00:24:46,320 --> 00:24:48,480
That's right! Nobody fessed up.

481
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:50,440
The killer broke the vase?

482
00:24:50,880 --> 00:24:52,680
But we examined the shards

483
00:24:52,760 --> 00:24:54,560
and found no fingerprints or skin tissues.

484
00:24:54,680 --> 00:24:58,000
I still think Tsang Chun-kit and
Hung Tzi-long are the prime suspects.

485
00:24:58,080 --> 00:24:59,640
Because they're in charge of the cylinders.

486
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:02,760
Someone swapped the cylinder
that killed Ngai Ka-yan.

487
00:25:02,880 --> 00:25:05,480
It would appear they had nothing
to do with it.

488
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:07,280
Talking about a motive,

489
00:25:07,360 --> 00:25:09,720
Tsang Chun-kit is definitely
the prime suspect.

490
00:25:09,920 --> 00:25:12,120
Is it possible when they were
making the stink bombs,

491
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:13,840
they made an extra one with
a high concentration of H2S

492
00:25:13,920 --> 00:25:15,440
then swap it again

493
00:25:15,520 --> 00:25:17,040
to kill Ngai Ka-yan?

494
00:25:17,120 --> 00:25:19,360
Let's focus on those two.

495
00:25:24,360 --> 00:25:25,000
Ko Sir!

496
00:25:25,080 --> 00:25:26,040
Cheong...

497
00:25:26,080 --> 00:25:29,840
The Commercial Crime Bureau called me today
and asked about Ngai Ka-yan.

498
00:25:30,080 --> 00:25:31,320
Why the CCB?

499
00:25:31,400 --> 00:25:33,560
They're onto a businessman called Fung To,

500
00:25:33,680 --> 00:25:35,080
who goes by the nickname Cigarette To,

501
00:25:35,160 --> 00:25:37,680
who's suspected of using shell companies
to launder money.

502
00:25:37,760 --> 00:25:39,440
He often placed ads with online channels

503
00:25:39,520 --> 00:25:41,720
or title sponsored their content
with loads of money.

504
00:25:41,800 --> 00:25:43,600
The money is linked to Ngai Ka-yan?

505
00:25:43,680 --> 00:25:45,800
These shell companies had
frequent transactions

506
00:25:45,880 --> 00:25:48,600
with 8 accounts under Ngai Kan-yan's name.

507
00:25:48,720 --> 00:25:50,200
Typical kickback.

508
00:25:50,360 --> 00:25:51,640
Now we have a new lead,

509
00:25:51,800 --> 00:25:53,440
all thanks to the CCB.

510
00:25:53,520 --> 00:25:57,320
They have been tailing Cigarette To
for a long time.

511
00:25:57,360 --> 00:25:58,920
This guy's operation is watertight.

512
00:25:58,960 --> 00:26:01,640
But someone got into a fight in his office

513
00:26:01,760 --> 00:26:03,280
and that's how word got out.

514
00:26:03,400 --> 00:26:05,080
And that someone was Ngai Ka-yan?

515
00:26:05,160 --> 00:26:08,720
Ngai Ka-yan and Tsang Chun-kit
got into a fist fight.

516
00:26:09,440 --> 00:26:11,680
Tsang Chun-kit is getting kickback too?

517
00:26:11,800 --> 00:26:14,360
The power struggle at the channel is fake.

518
00:26:14,440 --> 00:26:16,200
The real motive was over money.

519
00:26:16,320 --> 00:26:19,000
Better question them again.

520
00:26:19,080 --> 00:26:21,160
Hung Tzi-long may know something too.

521
00:26:21,240 --> 00:26:23,280
Why bother? They must be partners in crime.

522
00:26:23,360 --> 00:26:24,800
You're seldom so certain about something.

523
00:26:24,880 --> 00:26:28,640
Because our TCD colleagues decrypted the
computers of the channel staff.

524
00:26:28,760 --> 00:26:31,640
There's more to Hung Tzi-long
than meets the eye.

525
00:26:31,800 --> 00:26:33,960
This is a screen cap of a chat group.

526
00:26:34,040 --> 00:26:35,720
We found this on your computer.

527
00:26:35,840 --> 00:26:37,520
How do you explain that?

528
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:41,960
Where did this come from?

529
00:26:42,040 --> 00:26:43,400
I never opened this account

530
00:26:43,440 --> 00:26:44,880
or asked these questions.

531
00:26:44,960 --> 00:26:48,440
Seven days ago, you DM'd a
high school Chemistry teacher.

532
00:26:48,520 --> 00:26:51,040
You asked, "Can you make H2S?"

533
00:26:51,120 --> 00:26:53,760
"Do you have details?" "Can you teach me?"

534
00:26:53,880 --> 00:26:57,400
He replied, "Yes, you need simple tools."

535
00:26:57,480 --> 00:26:59,080
"What do you need it for?"

536
00:26:59,120 --> 00:27:00,440
You said it was for teaching.

537
00:27:00,520 --> 00:27:03,800
He asked you, "Are you teaching
students? Be careful."

538
00:27:03,880 --> 00:27:06,400
"Kids don't know any better,"

539
00:27:06,480 --> 00:27:07,840
"there may be accidents"

540
00:27:07,920 --> 00:27:12,120
"because high concentration of H2S
is dangerous and lethal.

541
00:27:12,360 --> 00:27:14,360
Sir, I didn't ask any of that.

542
00:27:14,480 --> 00:27:17,800
I didn't know high concentration of
hydrogen sulfide is lethal.

543
00:27:17,920 --> 00:27:19,200
Did I say hydrogen sulfide?

544
00:27:19,280 --> 00:27:22,240
I know H2S is hydrogen sulfide.

545
00:27:22,320 --> 00:27:23,440
But I didn't know...

546
00:27:23,480 --> 00:27:25,880
This conversation can prove you're lying.

547
00:27:25,920 --> 00:27:27,320
Save your crap for the judge.

548
00:27:27,480 --> 00:27:30,120
No...what must I say before
you'll believe me?

549
00:27:31,760 --> 00:27:34,080
Where did you and Paul learn how
to make a stink bomb?

550
00:27:42,240 --> 00:27:45,680
I bought everything. What about the formula?

551
00:27:46,160 --> 00:27:47,200
Done.

552
00:27:48,080 --> 00:27:49,800
I remember now...

553
00:27:49,960 --> 00:27:52,480
Tom and I were making the stink bombs
in a factory building.

554
00:27:52,640 --> 00:27:55,360
Ask him, he used my computer
to search online.

555
00:27:55,440 --> 00:27:57,120
He can clear me.

556
00:27:57,280 --> 00:27:59,120
No, I didn't use his computer.

557
00:27:59,440 --> 00:28:02,320
Your statement is bad for Hung Tzi-long.

558
00:28:02,400 --> 00:28:03,880
You're sure you didn't remember it wrong?

559
00:28:03,960 --> 00:28:05,320
No.

560
00:28:05,600 --> 00:28:07,880
OK. Now it's your turn.

561
00:28:08,080 --> 00:28:09,760
Did you know beforehand about Ngai Ka-yan

562
00:28:09,840 --> 00:28:13,560
getting kickbacks from Fung To,
a.k.a. Cigarette To?

563
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:15,200
Why do you ask?

564
00:28:15,320 --> 00:28:17,760
You were irresponsive to our questions

565
00:28:17,840 --> 00:28:19,000
and gave us the run around.

566
00:28:19,120 --> 00:28:22,040
Look at your reaction when
we mentioned kickbacks.

567
00:28:22,120 --> 00:28:23,560
What are you hiding?

568
00:28:25,320 --> 00:28:26,120
Don't try to frame me.

569
00:28:26,240 --> 00:28:27,480
I didn't take any kickbacks.

570
00:28:27,600 --> 00:28:31,360
But your fight with Ngai Ka-yan
in Cigarette To's office

571
00:28:31,440 --> 00:28:32,840
is the talk of the town.

572
00:28:33,480 --> 00:28:36,320
Jerk! How dare you tread on my turf!

573
00:28:36,440 --> 00:28:38,520
I learnt the dirty tricks from you, scumbag!

574
00:28:38,600 --> 00:28:40,320
If I knew you'd be such a mad dog,

575
00:28:40,360 --> 00:28:41,800
I wouldn't have brought you on board.

576
00:28:42,080 --> 00:28:43,360
I should let you die on the streets.

577
00:28:43,440 --> 00:28:44,880
Keep up with your pranks.

578
00:28:44,920 --> 00:28:46,400
You don't need a mad dog like me
to bite you.

579
00:28:46,480 --> 00:28:47,960
You'll do it to yourself eventually.

580
00:28:48,080 --> 00:28:48,680
What are you talking about?

581
00:28:48,760 --> 00:28:49,560
What?
What?

582
00:28:49,720 --> 00:28:53,560
Stop! Don't fight...You just want money.

583
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:57,040
You want to fight Ngai Ka-yan
for Cigarette To's kickback,

584
00:28:57,120 --> 00:28:59,560
that's why there's a grudge between
you and Ngai Ka-yan.

585
00:28:59,680 --> 00:29:02,160
But Ngai Ka-yan preempted you.

586
00:29:02,280 --> 00:29:05,640
That's why you and Paul made a cylinder
of a high concentration of H2S

587
00:29:05,720 --> 00:29:07,600
and killed him during the livestreaming.

588
00:29:08,880 --> 00:29:10,240
I did not.

589
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:13,960
Well? Did Tom clear my name?

590
00:29:14,760 --> 00:29:18,160
He insisted he never touched your computer.

591
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:22,280
Tsang Chun-kit, why did you lie?

592
00:29:38,040 --> 00:29:40,320
You have nothing to say to me?

593
00:29:41,440 --> 00:29:43,360
Why did you drag me in?

594
00:29:43,560 --> 00:29:46,800
Why did you deny using my computer
to learn how to make H2S?

595
00:29:46,840 --> 00:29:49,240
You meant to use me as the scapegoat
from the start?

596
00:29:49,400 --> 00:29:51,960
I treated you like my pal, but you treated
me like a fool.

597
00:29:52,320 --> 00:29:54,280
You did it once and you did it again.

598
00:29:54,680 --> 00:29:57,320
Each time I hit rock bottom,
I have you to thank.

599
00:29:57,920 --> 00:29:59,480
(Two years ago)

600
00:30:00,800 --> 00:30:05,200
Tsang Chun-kit, you swore to me
the goods are in high demand,

601
00:30:05,240 --> 00:30:06,320
that's why I bought them.

602
00:30:06,400 --> 00:30:09,000
But nobody wanted it. I want my money back.

603
00:30:09,080 --> 00:30:10,480
What? Don't be absurd!

604
00:30:11,640 --> 00:30:13,000
Where did you get that watch?

605
00:30:13,080 --> 00:30:14,000
I have known you for years,

606
00:30:14,080 --> 00:30:16,600
you conned me just to buy this?

607
00:30:16,680 --> 00:30:17,920
Get your hands off me.

608
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:19,240
You scratch it, you pay for it.

609
00:30:19,280 --> 00:30:21,120
Return the goods. I only want my money.

610
00:30:21,160 --> 00:30:23,040
Return? You want to return them
because you can't sell them?

611
00:30:23,080 --> 00:30:23,840
You're out of your mind!

612
00:30:23,920 --> 00:30:26,800
No? Give me the watch. I'll sell it.

613
00:30:26,920 --> 00:30:29,520
Hey...

614
00:30:33,680 --> 00:30:35,120
It's a fake!

615
00:30:36,040 --> 00:30:37,360
I never said it was real.

616
00:30:37,440 --> 00:30:41,120
Are you just as big a sucker as I am?

617
00:30:47,280 --> 00:30:49,200
We're already in debt,

618
00:30:49,240 --> 00:30:52,120
why drink this expensive beer?

619
00:30:53,040 --> 00:30:55,120
You rather be sober and owe $600K?

620
00:30:55,240 --> 00:30:58,640
Or be drunk and owe $600K plus $500?

621
00:30:59,600 --> 00:31:00,920
Take another swig.

622
00:31:02,880 --> 00:31:05,640
If I run into someone like this
at the TV station,

623
00:31:05,720 --> 00:31:06,960
I'd make an about turn.

624
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:09,360
But when you said you had perks for me,

625
00:31:09,440 --> 00:31:12,040
I truly believed you and bought the stuff.

626
00:31:12,120 --> 00:31:14,440
I won't feel guilty about it.

627
00:31:14,600 --> 00:31:19,360
We've been had because we were greedy
and deserved what we got.

628
00:31:19,640 --> 00:31:20,960
Here...

629
00:31:21,920 --> 00:31:25,880
Wait...you had speaking parts in
several comedies

630
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:28,080
and the response was good.

631
00:31:28,240 --> 00:31:29,800
Why did you get into pyramid selling?

632
00:31:29,920 --> 00:31:32,800
You know we live from paycheck
to paycheck in this business.

633
00:31:32,920 --> 00:31:35,280
I was looking for a backup plan

634
00:31:35,320 --> 00:31:36,960
but got scammed.

635
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:38,880
You're quite gifted as an actor.

636
00:31:38,960 --> 00:31:40,440
You shouldn't end up like this.

637
00:31:40,520 --> 00:31:42,920
Yeah...in a few years,

638
00:31:42,960 --> 00:31:44,880
our names will be on online charts of

639
00:31:44,920 --> 00:31:51,080
top ten talented bit part actors.

640
00:31:51,640 --> 00:31:54,240
At least people recognize us.

641
00:31:54,400 --> 00:31:55,720
I don't mind waiting

642
00:31:55,840 --> 00:31:58,040
as long as I can continue to act.

643
00:31:58,160 --> 00:32:01,040
Let's hope the loan sharks
won't kill us first.

644
00:32:01,680 --> 00:32:04,080
Can you be more positive?

645
00:32:04,200 --> 00:32:06,160
We were greedy this time,

646
00:32:06,200 --> 00:32:08,640
if we keep our feet on the ground,

647
00:32:08,720 --> 00:32:10,280
I'm sure we can turn things around.

648
00:32:10,360 --> 00:32:13,200
OK...you'll be my witness.

649
00:32:14,240 --> 00:32:17,080
I, Tsang Chun-kit, do solemnly swear,

650
00:32:17,120 --> 00:32:18,560
I'll never be greedy again

651
00:32:18,640 --> 00:32:21,000
or let anyone else con me again.

652
00:32:21,760 --> 00:32:24,520
That's so corny, but I like it.

653
00:32:24,840 --> 00:32:26,360
I, Hung Tzi-long, do solemnly swear,

654
00:32:26,480 --> 00:32:28,720
I'll never let Tsang Chun-kit con me again.

655
00:32:28,760 --> 00:32:32,000
You should pray that you won't let
other people con you.

656
00:32:33,160 --> 00:32:34,920
Let's both swear, as pals

657
00:32:35,040 --> 00:32:37,200
we'll never let anyone con us again.

658
00:32:37,480 --> 00:32:38,320
OK!

659
00:32:38,480 --> 00:32:41,720
We'll never let anyone con us again.

660
00:32:52,920 --> 00:32:55,400
I never expected working for Jarvis

661
00:32:55,440 --> 00:32:57,520
would make me famous and make money.

662
00:32:57,640 --> 00:32:59,800
We pull pranks on people,

663
00:32:59,920 --> 00:33:02,480
but we never hurt anyone.

664
00:33:02,640 --> 00:33:06,080
We wanted to act and we did it.

665
00:33:06,240 --> 00:33:08,840
I was really having a good time.

666
00:33:09,320 --> 00:33:11,120
Jarvis has changed too.

667
00:33:11,200 --> 00:33:13,320
He became callous and he set us up.

668
00:33:13,480 --> 00:33:16,440
I'm afraid we'll become like him some day.

669
00:33:16,760 --> 00:33:19,520
Luckily, you came forward every time
and stood up to him.

670
00:33:22,320 --> 00:33:25,360
I really thought you were a kindred spirit.

671
00:33:25,480 --> 00:33:27,480
But you only wanted to hurt me.

672
00:33:27,640 --> 00:33:28,800
He didn't clear your name,

673
00:33:28,880 --> 00:33:30,360
because he wanted to steal from Ngai Ka-yan

674
00:33:30,440 --> 00:33:32,880
a business tycoon called Cigarette To.

675
00:33:32,960 --> 00:33:35,160
He wanted the kickbacks for himself.

676
00:33:35,280 --> 00:33:36,720
But Ngai Ka-yan saw through him.

677
00:33:36,840 --> 00:33:38,640
That's why he wanted him dead.

678
00:33:38,800 --> 00:33:42,320
You pretended to get even with Jarvis
by pulling a prank on him.

679
00:33:42,400 --> 00:33:45,360
But you have an ulterior motive.

680
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:48,280
You wanted to use me to kill him,

681
00:33:48,480 --> 00:33:51,480
then you can get kickbacks for yourself.

682
00:33:53,360 --> 00:33:55,280
We swore we'd be brothers,

683
00:33:55,360 --> 00:33:57,640
but you played me for a fool.

684
00:33:59,600 --> 00:34:01,600
I know it's hard for you to believe me.

685
00:34:01,680 --> 00:34:03,040
But I did not.

686
00:34:03,440 --> 00:34:05,200
Then why didn't you clear my name?

687
00:34:06,440 --> 00:34:07,880
Cat got your tongue?

688
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:10,560
You're holding out on me,
how do you expect me to believe you?

689
00:34:10,640 --> 00:34:14,760
I'm sorry. But something bad will happen
if I told the truth.

690
00:34:15,280 --> 00:34:18,840
What could be worse than me
being accused of murder?

691
00:34:23,720 --> 00:34:25,240
Relax!

692
00:34:25,520 --> 00:34:27,200
You volunteered to give a statement

693
00:34:27,280 --> 00:34:28,800
only to help your pal?

694
00:34:30,320 --> 00:34:33,040
But I'll be hurting someone I respect.

695
00:34:33,120 --> 00:34:34,800
From a business perspective,

696
00:34:34,840 --> 00:34:38,120
Jarvis is making money for the company

697
00:34:38,200 --> 00:34:41,400
and advertisers trust him.

698
00:34:42,520 --> 00:34:45,280
To put it nicely, I'm in charge of Little J.

699
00:34:45,520 --> 00:34:50,720
But Jarvis actually calls the shots.

700
00:34:50,800 --> 00:34:55,800
Hegemony is not exactly healthy
for the company.

701
00:34:56,200 --> 00:34:59,400
Perhaps...I can be useful to you.

702
00:34:59,480 --> 00:35:01,280
He's holding out on the advertisers.

703
00:35:01,360 --> 00:35:04,440
Most of the money came from Cigarette To.

704
00:35:04,600 --> 00:35:06,280
This guy is a known miser.

705
00:35:06,400 --> 00:35:10,480
Why would he spend so much money
on our channel?

706
00:35:10,720 --> 00:35:12,200
You suspect Jarvis is accepting kickbacks?

707
00:35:12,280 --> 00:35:16,160
I can't go after our bread winner.

708
00:35:16,320 --> 00:35:18,720
Leave that to me. I'll get the evidence.

709
00:35:19,560 --> 00:35:23,320
One day, while Mr. Tsui summoned
Jarvis to a meeting,

710
00:35:23,400 --> 00:35:25,720
I made a copy of his transaction record

711
00:35:25,760 --> 00:35:28,360
and gave it to Mr. Tsui.

712
00:35:30,840 --> 00:35:31,880
Mr. Tsui.

713
00:35:31,960 --> 00:35:34,200
You're no longer at Jarvis' disposal.

714
00:35:35,760 --> 00:35:37,920
I went through the numbers carefully.

715
00:35:38,040 --> 00:35:39,600
Each time Jarvis gets a kickback,

716
00:35:39,720 --> 00:35:42,400
he'd transfer money into your bank account.

717
00:35:42,560 --> 00:35:44,200
I realized the gravity of the matter

718
00:35:44,240 --> 00:35:46,080
and am still deciding what to do.

719
00:35:46,320 --> 00:35:48,480
I like you from the start,

720
00:35:48,560 --> 00:35:50,920
that's why I've been grooming you,

721
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:53,080
hoping when you're ready,

722
00:35:53,160 --> 00:35:55,320
you can help me keep Jarvis in line.

723
00:35:56,200 --> 00:35:58,520
I'm glad you didn't let me down.

724
00:35:59,120 --> 00:36:02,480
In the end, I gave him the USB.

725
00:36:03,120 --> 00:36:05,200
Jarvis no longer has anything on Mr. Tsui,

726
00:36:05,240 --> 00:36:06,360
that's why he decided to take a chance

727
00:36:06,480 --> 00:36:08,280
and told me to approach Cigarette To

728
00:36:08,320 --> 00:36:09,960
to inform him we don't allow kickbacks.

729
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:11,600
If you never accepted any kickbacks,

730
00:36:11,760 --> 00:36:14,160
then you don't have a motive
to kill Ngai Ka-yan.

731
00:36:14,280 --> 00:36:16,320
Why did you use Hung Tzi-long's computer

732
00:36:16,400 --> 00:36:17,720
to look up how to make the lethal gas

733
00:36:17,800 --> 00:36:18,880
and frame him for it?

734
00:36:19,880 --> 00:36:23,640
It wasn't me who used the computer.

735
00:36:23,880 --> 00:36:27,520
All set. The high school teacher agreed
to give use the H2S formula.

736
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:30,000
You really want to increase
the H2S concentration?

737
00:36:30,120 --> 00:36:31,520
I'm worried something bad would happen.

738
00:36:31,560 --> 00:36:33,920
We have different sources that confirmed

739
00:36:33,960 --> 00:36:36,880
a higher concentration will only
make you excited,

740
00:36:36,960 --> 00:36:40,920
sting the eyes and cause nausea.

741
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:43,120
It's far from being lethal.

742
00:36:43,240 --> 00:36:46,920
Our intention was to trick Jarvis,
I'm afraid...

743
00:36:47,600 --> 00:36:50,360
But a stink bomb has no impact.

744
00:36:50,480 --> 00:36:52,600
Making him teary-eyed and cough

745
00:36:52,680 --> 00:36:55,040
won't convince Cigarette To that
Jarvis' way is passe

746
00:36:55,080 --> 00:36:58,080
and he's no longer the king of pranks.

747
00:36:58,160 --> 00:37:00,520
It won't convince him to deal with us.

748
00:37:00,640 --> 00:37:02,160
But...

749
00:37:02,240 --> 00:37:04,280
Increase the concentration a bit.

750
00:37:04,400 --> 00:37:08,200
Make Jarvis shoot of his mouth
in front of the camera.

751
00:37:08,360 --> 00:37:13,440
It'll be fine. You're a smart guy. Bye.

752
00:37:22,320 --> 00:37:23,560
You followed the formula,

753
00:37:23,720 --> 00:37:24,760
kept Hung Tzi-long in the dark

754
00:37:24,840 --> 00:37:27,480
and increased the H2S concentration.

755
00:37:27,520 --> 00:37:29,760
Between 1:50 p.m. and 2:00 p.m.,

756
00:37:29,840 --> 00:37:32,120
you claimed you were in the supplies room

757
00:37:32,160 --> 00:37:33,840
and you went to the toilet.

758
00:37:33,920 --> 00:37:35,480
That was a lie.

759
00:37:35,560 --> 00:37:38,840
You went inside Ngai Ka-yan's office
to swap the cylinder, right?

760
00:37:38,920 --> 00:37:42,200
No...I was lying.

761
00:37:43,640 --> 00:37:45,480
I wasn't in the supplies room.

762
00:37:46,360 --> 00:37:48,120
I was in the storeroom.

763
00:37:49,200 --> 00:37:50,960
I needed to protect myself.

764
00:37:51,120 --> 00:37:53,680
I printed and kept a copy of
the transaction record.

765
00:37:53,920 --> 00:37:55,960
But since my big fight with Jarvis,

766
00:37:56,080 --> 00:37:57,800
I was worried he might find the hard copy.

767
00:37:57,920 --> 00:38:00,000
So I shredded it in the office.

768
00:38:02,440 --> 00:38:03,640
When I was down to the last few pages,

769
00:38:03,720 --> 00:38:05,240
I heard something broke in the hallway,

770
00:38:05,400 --> 00:38:06,920
I was worried about getting caught.

771
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:08,280
So I went outside to take a look

772
00:38:08,360 --> 00:38:09,760
and I saw Paul...
Who broke this?

773
00:38:09,840 --> 00:38:10,840
I don't know.

774
00:38:10,920 --> 00:38:13,360
I was in the supplies room checking
the props of the Challenge.

775
00:38:13,560 --> 00:38:16,480
The point is, I didn't listen to Mr. Tsui.

776
00:38:16,560 --> 00:38:18,040
I didn't make a cylinder with
a higher concentration.

777
00:38:18,120 --> 00:38:19,640
I only meant to trick Jarvis,

778
00:38:19,720 --> 00:38:21,600
I didn't want to hurt anyone.

779
00:38:21,640 --> 00:38:23,800
I only made an ordinary stink bomb.

780
00:38:23,920 --> 00:38:26,280
The one Jarvis used was not mine.

781
00:38:26,360 --> 00:38:27,720
Then it must be Mr. Tsui.

782
00:38:27,800 --> 00:38:29,560
He found out you didn't listen to him,

783
00:38:29,640 --> 00:38:31,640
he made one himself.

784
00:38:31,760 --> 00:38:33,280
I don't think he did it.

785
00:38:33,400 --> 00:38:35,240
He didn't show up at the channel that day.

786
00:38:35,320 --> 00:38:36,360
How did he swap it?

787
00:38:36,440 --> 00:38:37,760
Mr. Tsui didn't show up

788
00:38:37,840 --> 00:38:40,160
but he could have an accomplice.

789
00:38:40,200 --> 00:38:41,960
And it was you.

790
00:38:43,000 --> 00:38:44,400
You said you didn't do it,

791
00:38:44,520 --> 00:38:47,360
did you see anyone break the vase?

792
00:38:47,440 --> 00:38:49,440
Or anyone in and out of
Ngai Ka-yan's office?

793
00:38:49,480 --> 00:38:51,920
No. I told you everything I know.

794
00:38:52,080 --> 00:38:54,520
You should know what you just said,

795
00:38:54,600 --> 00:38:57,440
cannot clear you as a murder suspect.

796
00:38:58,080 --> 00:39:01,920
I know. I only told you everything

797
00:39:02,040 --> 00:39:04,600
because I don't want to implicate Paul.

798
00:39:07,920 --> 00:39:09,920
Try to answer all the messages
sent to the channel.

799
00:39:10,160 --> 00:39:11,720
Whatever they said,

800
00:39:11,800 --> 00:39:13,160
we have a duty to respond.

801
00:39:13,280 --> 00:39:15,480
I'll speak to Helen about wrapping up
the livestreaming.

802
00:39:15,520 --> 00:39:16,960
OK!
OK!

803
00:39:17,120 --> 00:39:18,880
Hey!
Paul?

804
00:39:19,040 --> 00:39:20,560
They let you out?

805
00:39:21,160 --> 00:39:22,040
Where's Tom?

806
00:39:22,080 --> 00:39:23,520
Still in custody.

807
00:39:23,640 --> 00:39:25,120
He swapped Jarvis' cylinder?

808
00:39:25,160 --> 00:39:27,120
You knew?

809
00:39:27,280 --> 00:39:28,640
Daisy told us.

810
00:39:29,000 --> 00:39:31,160
The Police investigation is still on.

811
00:39:31,320 --> 00:39:35,280
Within those ten minutes, I had an alibi.

812
00:39:35,360 --> 00:39:39,000
Tom admitted the stink bomb was his idea.

813
00:39:39,120 --> 00:39:42,040
The Police let me go because
I'm the least likely suspect.

814
00:39:42,160 --> 00:39:44,520
Why was Mr. Tsui brought in
for questioning?

815
00:39:44,640 --> 00:39:46,720
The Police suspect Mr. Tsui had
a disagreement with Jarvis

816
00:39:46,840 --> 00:39:49,680
that prompted him to resort to murder.

817
00:39:49,720 --> 00:39:51,440
But they didn't have enough to charge him

818
00:39:51,520 --> 00:39:55,360
because he was in a client meeting
the whole day

819
00:39:55,480 --> 00:39:57,560
and was not at the scene.

820
00:39:57,600 --> 00:40:00,360
They could only charge him for
conspiring to murder.

821
00:40:00,400 --> 00:40:02,360
Tom is still the prime suspect.

822
00:40:02,400 --> 00:40:03,920
Did Tom do it?

823
00:40:04,120 --> 00:40:05,880
I have no proof.

824
00:40:06,000 --> 00:40:07,840
But I have known him long enough,

825
00:40:07,920 --> 00:40:09,280
he's nothing like that.

826
00:40:09,360 --> 00:40:10,840
Looks can be deceiving.

827
00:40:12,640 --> 00:40:14,280
I'm glad you're back.

828
00:40:14,360 --> 00:40:16,400
You can help run Little J Media.

829
00:40:16,680 --> 00:40:18,240
But Auntie Ching quit.

830
00:40:18,360 --> 00:40:19,600
Why?

831
00:40:19,760 --> 00:40:22,680
She's been having nightmares
since Jarvis died.

832
00:40:22,760 --> 00:40:24,560
She'll be here till month end.

833
00:40:24,640 --> 00:40:28,160
Who'd want to stay and be reminded of him?

834
00:40:28,440 --> 00:40:29,960
You want to leave too?

835
00:40:30,480 --> 00:40:34,120
You never agreed with Jarvis' style.

836
00:40:34,200 --> 00:40:37,400
Go ahead, let the channel fall apart.

837
00:40:37,520 --> 00:40:40,280
Let Jarvis' effort go to waste.

838
00:40:42,600 --> 00:40:43,800
(Three months after the incident)

839
00:40:43,880 --> 00:40:45,240
I didn't expect there's a case within
Ngai Ka-yan's case.

840
00:40:45,320 --> 00:40:47,480
Too bad we don't have enough to
charge Mr. Tsui.

841
00:40:47,600 --> 00:40:50,040
I've been digging these past three months,

842
00:40:50,160 --> 00:40:51,800
but we have no solid proof.

843
00:40:51,840 --> 00:40:55,000
Tom and Mr. Tsui are
particularly suspicious.

844
00:40:55,080 --> 00:40:58,160
Within those ten minutes before
Ngai Ka-yan left with the lethal gas,

845
00:40:58,240 --> 00:41:02,160
no one could verify the exact position
of the other five people.

846
00:41:02,360 --> 00:41:04,800
I still think Tsang Chun-kit
is the prime suspect.

847
00:41:04,880 --> 00:41:06,800
Was he being unusually honest

848
00:41:06,880 --> 00:41:08,720
and volunteered everything about Mr. Tsui?

849
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:12,040
Or he did it to cover up a bigger lie?

850
00:41:12,360 --> 00:41:14,880
This is too brain burning.

851
00:41:14,920 --> 00:41:16,840
I can't take this anymore.

852
00:41:16,960 --> 00:41:21,720
These kids may have the answer for us.

853
00:41:22,240 --> 00:41:24,640
Yo, it's Agent J again.

854
00:41:24,680 --> 00:41:27,040
We have a new game for you.

855
00:41:27,120 --> 00:41:30,040
It's called Pick Your Pigswill.

856
00:41:30,120 --> 00:41:31,720
Here, we have two buckets,

857
00:41:31,800 --> 00:41:35,400
one is water, the other is pigswill.

858
00:41:35,520 --> 00:41:37,920
If you pick the bucket with the water,

859
00:41:38,000 --> 00:41:41,640
you'll get $20K and other prizes.

860
00:41:41,680 --> 00:41:44,160
Without further ado, let's begin...

861
00:41:51,600 --> 00:41:53,120
They're both pigswill!

862
00:41:54,360 --> 00:41:55,720
What are you doing?

863
00:41:55,800 --> 00:41:57,760
Split!
Run...

864
00:41:57,800 --> 00:41:59,200
Are you OK?

865
00:42:20,280 --> 00:42:23,360
This pin is the same as the one
found in Ngai Ka-yan's office.

866
00:42:23,480 --> 00:42:25,600
Is it connected to his death?

867
00:42:26,080 --> 00:42:27,840
Why do they have this pin?
